== Prep corn husks ==

Add enough warm-hot water in a large #bowl{} or clean #sink{} to cover your @corn husks{10%large}(soaked in warm water). This step takes a few minutes to make the corn husk pliable.

> Optional: Extra corn husks to make thin strips to tie the tamales.

== Make masa dough ==

Place @unsalted butter{1/2%cup}(at room temperature) and @sugar{6%Tbs} in a medium-sized bowl and, with the help of a #mixer{}, beat for ~{2%minutes} until it has a creamy texture.

In a different bowl, mix @Masa Harina{1 1/2%cup}, @baking powder{1/4%teaspoon}, and add @raisins{2%Tbs}. Stir well, and then add the @warm water{1 1/2%cup} little by little.

While mixing the dry ingredients with the water, add @red or pink food coloring{6%drops}. Mix well to have a uniform color.

Now, add the butter and sugar mixture.

Beat the dough with your hands or a #wooden spoon{}, as the dough is sometimes too heavy to work with your mixer unless you have a heavy-duty #Stand Mixer{} like Kitchen Aid.

> Tip: The dough will be ready when it looks fluffy and creamy, like very soft ice cream. If your dough seems too dry, add a little more water. The consistency has to be very soft.

== Assemble the tamales ==

Drain the corn husks from the soaking water; use a #kitchen towel{} to dry the excess water.

Now, place about ⅓ cup of corn masa over the extended corn husk.

Then, fold the edge of the husk around the filling, then fold the top down, like the pictures.

For a decorative presentation, you can wrap a string around the tamal.

Keep assembling the rest of the tamales.

== Steam sweet tamales ==

First, fill the bottom of the #steamer{} with about 1 to 2 inches of water. Then, insert the #steamer rack{} of your #tamalera{}.

Now, place the tamales standing up in your #steam pot{}.

After you are done placing all your tamales, cover them with remaining corn husks, @?aluminium foil{}, a #plastic bag{}, or a damp #towel{}, and then cover them with the #pot lid{}.

  Steam boil for ~{1 - 1 1/4%hours} at medium heat. Add more hot water if needed to avoid burning the tamales.

Enjoy!